  "synthetic_dataset_notes": {
    "is_synthetic": true,
    "generation_mechanism": "100% synthetic dataset with independent uniform features (max pairwise |r| < 0.03). 8,642/10,000 rows (86.42%) follow an exact 6-rule deterministic cascade: (1) N < 60 -> Urea (2,902 rows, 29.02%); (2) P < 40 -> DAP (2,738 rows, 27.38%); (3) K < 40 -> MOP (1,198 rows, 11.98%) \u2014 together N, P, and K drive 6,838/10,000 rows (68.38%); (4) pH < 5.5 -> Compost (798 rows, 7.98%); (5) pH > 7.8 -> Zinc Sulphate (553 rows, 5.53%); (6) Crop_Growth_Stage == 'Vegetative' -> NPK (453 rows, 4.53%). The remaining 1,358 rows (13.58%) are sampled approximately uniformly across all 7 classes.",
    "npk_rule_share": 0.6838,
    "bayes_ceiling_19_features": 0.8852,
    "bayes_ceiling_6_features": 0.3205,
    "accuracy_caveat": "SoilSense collects 4 soil sensors (Soil_pH, Electrical_Conductivity, Soil_Moisture, Temperature) plus Crop_Type and Soil_Type \u2014 Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium are NOT measured or supplied. Removing N, P, and K drops the first three cascade rules that drove 68.38% of labels in this synthetic CSV, collapsing the theoretical Bayes-optimal accuracy ceiling from ~88.52% (19 features) to ~32.05% (6 features). On this synthetic dataset, the 6-feature model primarily learns the pH rules (pH < 5.5 -> Compost at ~31.8% posterior; pH > 7.8 -> Zinc Sulphate at ~31.6% posterior) plus the neutral-pH majority class prior (Urea at ~32.3% posterior for 5.5 <= pH <= 7.8). Because top-class probabilities stay around 0.30-0.34 (below the default 0.55 low_confidence threshold), low_confidence=true flags these predictions honestly so downstream deterministic agronomic guidance can assist. Do NOT overstate accuracy; replace this synthetic dataset with real 4-sensor regional field-trial data whenever available.",
    "excluded_feature_rationale": "13 columns (Nitrogen_Level, Phosphorus_Level, Potassium_Level, Organic_Carbon, Humidity, Rainfall, Crop_Growth_Stage, Season, Irrigation_Type, Previous_Crop, Region, Fertilizer_Used_Last_Season, Yield_Last_Season) are excluded from the production 6-feature pipeline because SoilSense ESP32 hardware and soil sample workflows only supply 4 soil sensors (pH, EC, moisture, temperature) plus crop type and soil type. Excluding unavailable fields ensures production inference never fabricates missing N-P-K or lab values."
